  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-25 (dev 2399d5ad7c; owner-requested re-check of the 17 actionable open P2 violated INV/META items; fixtures archived under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_check_10252026/). VERDICT: STALE-TEXT; still violated. Fresh fake HOME/XDG: `trust-backend rust_analyzer proj` wrote state/hypergumbo/trust.d/<hash>.json (0600); `init-catalogs` wrote config/hypergumbo/README.md + 8 io_primitives.d/*.yaml; `run` under a real TTY with $HOME/hypergumbo present, answering y, wrote state/hypergumbo/offers.json (0644) and 3 files under <fake HOME>/hypergumbo/.hypergumbo-examples/ -- and analysing that $HOME/hypergumbo itself wrote them INTO THE ANALYSED REPOSITORY while the prompt said 'Nothing is written into any repository you analyse'. Raw writes: backend_trust.py:190/200/201, in_repo_catalogues.py:83/85/88, repo_tier_offer.py:143/146, 249/252, catalogue_home.py:391/396/405; offer hook still in main() (cli.py:13731/13738). Drift: write_repo_tier_examples now writes a `*` .gitignore in the examples tree (63a26c57c8, 10-16) -- fewer accidental commits, still a write. UNDER-SCOPED problem 2: not only the main() offer is outside every taint source -- diffing every def cmd_* against the catalogued *_sources.yaml finds 6 uncatalogued handlers: cmd_trust_backend (cli.py:3737), cmd_trust_catalogues (:3804), cmd_init_catalogs (:8129), cmd_backend_agreement, cmd_repeat_finder, cmd_catalog_inventory; so no claim covers any of the five write sites. Related: WI-kipid (same offer hook, UX side). NOT checked: the verify-claims caveat counts."  # 0323
